        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: AI safety event taxonomy — OTEL and Prometheus exporter mappings",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nThe AI safety event types defined in #107176 need to be wired to the existing OTEL and Prometheus exporters so operators can observe them in their telemetry stacks. Without exporter mappings, the events are emitted but invisible.\n\n## Evidence\n- `extensions/diagnostics-otel/src/service-events.ts` — switch/case dispatcher; new cases added for all 6 ai_safety.* types\n- `extensions/diagnostics-otel/src/service-recorders-ai-safety.ts` (new file) — recorder factories per event type\n- `extensions/diagnostics-prometheus/src/service.ts` — unified counter `openclaw_ai_safety_events_total{event_type,severity,channel}` with low-cardinality labels only (Prometheus 2048-series cap respected)\n- `assignOtelAiSafetyAttributes()` in `service-attributes.ts` mirrors the existing `assignOtelSecurityAttributes()` pattern\n- `tool_policy.decision` and existing `tool.execution.blocked` non-overlap documented in JSDoc\n- Depends on: #107176\n\n## Evidence — Clawsweeper re-review fixes (2026-07-14)\n\n**Provenance fix:** the six AI safety OTEL recorders in `service-recorders-ai-safety.ts` previously discarded `DiagnosticEventMetadata`. Each recorder now receives the metadata and attaches `openclaw.ai_safety.emitter_trusted` (from `metadata.trusted`) so operators can distinguish core-trusted emissions from plugin-emitted ones. The attribute is named `emitter_trusted` to avoid colliding with the pre-existing `openclaw.ai_safety.trusted` label on `external_content.consumed`, which describes content-source trust, not emitter provenance. The dispatcher in `service-events.ts` passes `metadata` through for all six `ai_safety.*` cases, matching the existing security-event recorder pattern.\n\n**Scope fix:** verified this branch introduces no `src/plugin-sdk/diagnostic-runtime.ts` changes of its own — the SDK type exports visible in the stacked diff come solely from the base contracts commits (#107176). No duplication to remove.\n\nLocal verification on this branch: `extensions/diagnostics-otel/src/service.test.ts` — 107 tests passed; `pnpm tsgo:extensions` clean.\n\n**4-PR series design note:** the security boundary is deliberate across the stack — #107176 defines the contracts and excludes AI safety events from the untrusted `emitDiagnosticEvent()` surface (type- and runtime-gated); this PR wires exporters and preserves emitter provenance; #107187 adds the only plugin-facing emission surface, gated by manifest `safetyEventTypes`; #107192 adds observability surfaces. Untrusted path gated, trusted path only.\n\n**OTEL note:** full end-to-end OTEL integration proof requires a running collector, which is not available in CI; recorder behavior is covered by the extension unit tests above.\n",
        "branch": "feat/ai-safety-exporters",
